        <mxCell id="e4b" edge="1" parent="1" source="eb" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeColor=#E7157B;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#232F3E;fontSize=11;" target="lambda" value="rule: source = aws.s3">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e5" edge="1" parent="1" source="lambda" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeColor=#545B64;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#232F3E;fontSize=11;" target="cw" value="logs each event">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#C8C8C8;fillColor=#F7F7F7;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#232F3E;spacing=8;" value="Notes&#xa;- Path 1 (Lambda), 2 (SNS), 3 (SQS) and 4 (EventBridge) are the four S3 Event Notification destinations.&#xa;- Path 4: S3 to EventBridge cannot filter at the source - filtering is done in the EventBridge rule.&#xa;- The other two of AWS&#39;s &#39;4 ways&#39; (S3 Object Lambda for request-time transforms, and S3 Storage Lens for metrics) are not event triggers and are covered in the README.&#xa;- All resource names derive from the ProjectName CloudFormation parameter - nothing is hardcoded." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="1220" x="100" y="660" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
